course: dictionary
lesson: 10687
title: Attacks with no cause
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Unprovoked» describes something that happens with no reason behind it. The other person did nothing to cause it. Look at the sentence around the word: «All sharks together make only about 70 unprovoked bites on people a year worldwide.» Ask yourself what the bites were caused by, and the clue points to nothing that the people did.
explain: The second sentence gives you a clue straight away: «unprovoked means nobody had poked, caught or fed the shark.» A shark that was not poked, caught or fed did nothing to start the bite. Try your meaning in the sentence: "about 70 bites that came with no reason" still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: The word often appears in phrases such as «an unprovoked attack» and «completely unprovoked». In school, hitting or being unkind to someone with no cause is unprovoked. The word tells you about the cause, not about how serious the action was.
fact: Unprovoked means happening without any reason, when the other person did nothing to cause it.
fact: «Unprovoked» is an adjective, and «an unprovoked attack» is a common phrase.
fact: «All sharks together make only about 70 unprovoked bites on people a year worldwide.»
fact: The second sentence explains it: «unprovoked means nobody had poked, caught or fed the shark.»
fact: A quick swap test: put "for no reason" in place of «unprovoked» and check that the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «He gave an unprovoked punch in the playground.» Why is the punch unprovoked? | *The other child had done nothing to cause it | The other child had called him names first | The teacher had asked him to do it | He was playing a game with a friend
exercise: Find and copy one word from this sentence that means happening without any reason: «All sharks together make only about 70 unprovoked bites on people a year worldwide.» | sharks | *unprovoked | bites | worldwide
exercise: The sentence says: «unprovoked means nobody had poked, caught or fed the shark.» What does unprovoked mean here? | Many sharks are in danger from fishing | It happened at night | *Nobody had poked, caught or fed the shark | The shark was very big
test: «Completely unprovoked, the boy pushed his friend off the bench.» What does unprovoked mean here? | The bench was wet | *The friend had done nothing to cause it | The boy was very tired | The friend had asked for help
test: Which word completes this phrase from the dictionary entry: an unprovoked ___? | afternoon | answer | apple | *attack
exam: What does «unprovoked» mean? | Happening after a long fight | Done by a whole group of people together | *Happening without any reason, when the other person did nothing to cause it | Very loud and sudden
